  "result": "I added the `docs-writer` subagent in `.claude/agents/docs-writer.md`.\n\n- **Model:** `haiku`, the fastest of the model aliases. `release-manager` uses the same one.\n- **No shell access:** its `tools` list is `Read, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write`. It can't run shell commands because `Bash` isn't in that list.\n- **Instructions:** it only edits `.md` files under `docs/`, reads the code before describing it, keeps the docs' existing style, and writes secrets as `${VAR}`.\n\nThe limit to `docs/` is only an instruction in the agent's prompt. Nothing technically stops it from editing files elsewhere. If you want that enforced, I can add a hook that blocks its edits outside `docs/`.\n\nI didn't run `npm run lint` or `npm run build`. This change only adds an agent config file, so it doesn't touch the app code those check.",
